{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.ShellClosureNormalForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.ShellClosureNormalForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FinCases","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.IntervalCases","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.nonclosure_ratio_moderate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.nonclosure_ratio_moderate","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L254-L259","doc":"Non-closures have moderate jumps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.closure_ratio_large","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.closure_ratio_large","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L247-L252","doc":"Shell closures have larger jumps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.dominant_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.dominant_coeff","kind":"def","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L233-L245","doc":"Dominant coefficient at each A. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.energy_jumps_after_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.energy_jumps_after_closure","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L224-L227","doc":"Energy jumps after closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.energy_drops_at_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.energy_drops_at_closure","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L219-L222","doc":"Energy drops at shell closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shell_gap_he4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shell_gap_he4","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L213-L217","doc":"Shell gap: ΔE(step 4) / ΔE(step 3) > 14. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hecke_energy_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hecke_energy_step","kind":"def","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L201-L211","doc":"The Hecke reduction energy at step k (adding k-th nucleon). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.li6_palindrome","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.li6_palindrome","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L189-L195","doc":"⁶Li(3,3) histogram is palindromic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.he4_palindrome","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.he4_palindrome","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L167-L172","doc":"⁴He histogram {1, 3, 4, 3, 1} is palindromic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.isPalindrome","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.isPalindrome","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L159-L165","doc":"A word-length histogram is palindromic if h(ℓ) = h(L - ℓ) for all ℓ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hecke_basis_size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hecke_basis_size","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L141-L153","doc":"The number of reduced words in H_A(q) is at most A!.\n(It equals A! when q is not a root of unity.)\n\n**Was an axiom; now proved (2026-11-15).** As stated it only asks for\n*some* finite set of normal-form words of size at most `A!`, and the\nempty set is one. The Kazhdan–Lusztig content (the reduced words form\na basis of size exactly `A!`) is open in Lean, bean `qou-n2un`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.sequential_build_always_normal_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.sequential_build_always_normal_form","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L123-L131","doc":"The sequential construction produces a normal form at every step.\nBy induction on A. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:shell-closure-normal-form","label":"prop:shell-closure-normal-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hopf_link_preserves_normal_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hopf_link_preserves_normal_form","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L108-L121","doc":"Inductive step: if N̄(A) is in normal form, then after Hopf-linking\none nucleon and applying the division algorithm, N̄(A+1) is also\nin normal form.\n\nThis follows immediately from the main theorem of Gröbner basis\ntheory: the division algorithm produces a normal form remainder\nfor ANY input, regardless of whether the input is already reduced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.identity_is_normal_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.identity_is_normal_form","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L101-L106","doc":"Base case: the identity element is in normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.division_terminates_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.division_terminates_unique","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L85-L99","doc":"The Gröbner division algorithm preserves well-foundedness.\nGiven any element of H_n(q), the division algorithm terminates\nand produces a unique normal form remainder.\n\n**Was an axiom; now proved (2026-11-15).** As stated, the conclusion\ndoes not mention `elem`, so it only says that *some* normal-form\nsupport exists, and the empty support is one. The intended content\n(the remainder of `elem` is in normal form, and it is unique) needs\nthe division algorithm itself and is open in Lean (bean `qou-n2un`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsNormalForm.no_yang_baxter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsNormalForm.no_yang_baxter","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L79-L79","doc":"No word contains σᵢσ_{i±1}σᵢ that is YB-reducible to a lex-smaller triple. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsNormalForm.no_far_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsNormalForm.no_far_comm","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L74-L74","doc":"No word contains σᵢσⱼ with i > j, |i-j| ≥ 2 (far-comm reducible). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsNormalForm.no_squares","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsNormalForm.no_squares","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L71-L71","doc":"No word contains σᵢσᵢ (Hecke reducible). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsNormalForm.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsNormalForm.mk","kind":"ctor","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IsNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IsNormalForm","kind":"structure","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/shell-closure-normal-form.lean#L65-L83","doc":"A Hecke element is in normal form if every word in its support\nis a reduced word: no σᵢ², no YB-reducible triples, no unsorted\nfar-commutativity pairs. ","signatureChunk":0}]}